Scoped notices for code adapted into src/mlx2/runtime/models/qwen4_attn_rows.py
(fused Qwen4 attention rows). See provenance/omlx-4052-qwen4-attn-rows.json for
paths, hashes and modifications.

1. omlx — Apache License 2.0
   Source: https://github.com/jundot/omlx PR #4052, head
   d05afc7a7a59a871531b89ee769460581a26aabb,
   omlx/patches/mlx_vlm_qwen4_exp_compat/vendor/mlx_vlm/models/qwen4_exp/attn_fused.py.
   The fused-row structure (q/k norm + RoPE in one launch per head and row;
   one-pass SDPA chains split over simdgroups and closed by a separate
   combine launch that also applies the output gate) is adapted from it.
   The full Apache-2.0 text is this repository's LICENSE.

2. MLX — MIT License (scoped to the arithmetic transcribed inside the Metal
   sources of qwen4_attn_rows.py: rms_single_row from rms_norm.metal,
   rope/rope_single from rope.metal, sdpa_vector / sdpa_vector_2pass_1 /
   sdpa_vector_2pass_2 from sdpa_vector.h, and select_sdpa_blocks from
   scaled_dot_product_attention.cpp, at ml-explore/mlx revision
   39400a0d4cf1641bc6e543cb5e3585757f491854)

